          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Dec 12 2023 22:34:40 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Cannulated screw systems</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\"><span class=\"fontsize-2em\">Stanley Asnis, MD invented the cannulated screw in the 1980’s, which became a major facilitator for advancing minimally invasive surgery in orthopaedics.<sup>1, 2</sup> The Asnis Micro cannulated screw systems enhances this legacy, offering dedicated screws for the foot and ankle surgeon.</span></span></p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon May 04 2026 16:52:01 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
        "text_copy_copy_copy": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "bottomPadding": "2",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-65eab19e7c@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-42b58e166b@example.invalid",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Tue Dec 12 2023 22:34:40 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">2.0 and 3.0mm titanium screw size options</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Low profile screw head may reduce potential soft-tissue irritation</span></li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Self-drilling/self-tapping design with a reverse cutting flute</span></li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Mon May 04 2026 16:51:20 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
